                <pb facs="0426" n="414" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg414"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51A/1186: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ford</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-26T10:00:00+03:25">June 26, 1944—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 26—9:48 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>457. Faced with responsibility of taking steps with possible grave repercussions,
                    Iranian economy [<hi rendition="#italic">Government?</hi>] is showing itself
                    reluctant to take steps that will force the departure of Millspaugh and his
                    mission. Legation has been informed that at secret session yesterday majority of
                    better elements of Majlis felt Millspaugh should stay under a system whereby a
                    council of Iranians would review his economic regulations before promulgation.
                    Millspaugh is to appear before Majlis today in secret session to discuss this
                    idea and it now appears possible that a <hi rendition="#italic">modus
                        vivendi</hi> may be worked out which will permit Millspaugh to remain.
                    Should this occur, it is difficult to see how Saed government could remain in
                    office and still enjoy the confidence of the Majlis and the people.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ford</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
